A tower tall, its light is shining bright,
It stands on the earth for miles to reach;
A symbol of hope and guidance in sight,
Its beacon fires up all night long.

The wind whistles through its metal gates,
As sailors gather round the ancient walls;
For they know that it will never falter,
When darkness falls or storms rage their way.

And so they listen with a calm and steady heart,
To find the sea's mysteries once more;
